// endpoint_list_log_sites.proto — ListLogSites: every log site that fired in
// a window of time, across every runtime, each with how often it fired, when
// it first and last did, and one record it wrote. AGENT API section. A pull,
// answered inside the caller's turn, for an agent asking what the system
// logged and what is new (`agent-repld logs sites -since WHEN`), and the read
// the production checks compare deploys with.
//
// A LOG SITE is one log call in source, named by its key: the first 12 hex of
// the sha256 of its runtime, the function the call is written in, and its
// template (logging-contract.md "Log sites"). Every record one call writes
// carries the same key, whatever values it renders, so counting by key counts
// what fired, not how many ways its values varied.
//
// THE ANSWER IS READ FROM THE DAEMON'S STORE, NEVER FROM THE LOGS. The daemon
// tallies every record of every sink into (deploy, site, level, hour) rows by
// a pass that reads each log file from its own cursor: before every removal
// of log files, at each deploy's start, and before every window is answered.
// So a window answers the same whether or not its log files still exist, and
// is current to the moment it is asked. Each row is credited to the
// deploy serving when its records were written. A window is therefore read at
// HOUR granularity: an hour the window only partly covers is counted whole,
